  "summary": "The code contained critical security and performance flaws, primarily due to unsafe file handling and lack of input validation. I have refactored the endpoint to use Flask's secure 'send_file' utility, applied PEP 8 naming conventions, and added type hints. The overall health is now significantly improved, though production deployment should still include rate limiting.",
  "fixed_code": "import os\nfrom flask import Flask, request, send_file, abort\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n# Define a safe base directory for file access\nSAFE_DIR = os.path.abspath(\"./data\")\n\n@app.route(\"/filedata\")\ndef get_file_data() -> bytes:\n    '''\n    Get the filename from the request argument,\n    validate the path, and return the file securely.\n    '''\n    filename = request.args.get('filename')\n    if not filename:\n        abort(400)\n\n    # Prevent path traversal\n    safe_path = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(SAFE_DIR, os.path.basename(filename)))\n    \n    if not safe_path.startswith(SAFE_DIR) or not os.path.exists(safe_path):\n        abort(404)\n\n    return send_file(safe_path)"
